FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/lsp.rs:1506 — CR-only line endings are not handled: `inside_comment` terminates a `//` comment only at `'\n'`, and `SourceMap::new` (same file) records only `'\n'` as a line start, while the lexer explicitly treats `'\r'` as a newline (src/lexer.rs:482-488). A file using classic-Mac `\r` endings therefore has every navigation call reject lines >1 as past EOF (or, on line 1, map columns across the whole file), and completions anywhere after a `//` are wrongly empty because the comment scan runs to EOF. — Add `'\r'`/CRLF handling to both the line-start builder and the comment terminator, and add a CR/CRLF navigation test. VERIFIED: traced both branches in source (not executed).
2. [MAJOR] src/lsp.rs:1355 — `goto_definition` falls back to a builtin whenever the identifier text matches `BUILTIN_NAMES`/`MODULES`, without consulting `member_names`. For `say holder.abs`, `abs` is recorded as a member access (line 1149) and is not the global builtin, yet goto answers `DefinitionKind::Builtin` at 0:0. `find_references` was fixed to exclude these (line 1397), so the two navigation APIs now disagree on the same token. — Guard the builtin fallback with `!member_names.contains(&index)` (note the test at line 1170 intentionally pins type-name `list` → builtin, so do not extend the guard to `type_names` without updating that test) and add a goto test on `holder.abs`.

